<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-6125] Enable updates on the same branch using dev/checkout_zeppelin_pr.sh</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-6125</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The `dev/checkout_zeppelin_pr.sh` script is useful for locally checking out PR commits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Currently, it fetches the PR and checks out a new branch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, if the script is run while already on the target branch, the updates are not reflected because `git checkout` does not move the `HEAD` when the current branch is already checked out.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To improve the script, it could be useful to allow updates when the current branch is already checked out, ensuring that changes could be reflected in the target branch.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
